     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><div>On Monday, January 23, 2017 at 1:20:35 PM UTC-5, Joe Cheng [RStudio] wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Isn&#39;t a shapefile actually an entire directory of files? (.shp, .shx, .dbf) Which one(s) are you uploading?</div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><div dir=\"ltr\">On Mon, Jan 23, 2017 at 9:52 AM Spencer Bell &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">sbel...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hello Everyone,</div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>I keep receiving &quot;Warning: Error in CPL_read_ogr: Open failed.&quot; when adding a shapefile in fileInput.</div><div><br></div><div>Does anyone have experience using the simple features package with shiny?</div><div><br></div><div>My code is below.</div><div><br></div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Thank you.</div></div><div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><div>server.R</div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sf</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">leaflet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>options</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">maxRequestSize</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#066\">30</span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#066\">1024</span><span style=\"color:#660\">^</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># use the below options code if you wish to increase the file input limit, in this example file input limit is increased from 5MB to 9MB</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\"># options(shiny.maxRequestSize = 9*1024^2)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br><br>shinyServer</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">function</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">input</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">output</span><span style=\"color:#660\">){</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># This reactive function will take the inputs from UI.R and use them for read.table() to read the data from the file. It returns the dataset in the form of a dataframe.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># file$datapath -&gt; gives the path of the file</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  <br>  data </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> reactive</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    file1 </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> input$file<br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">null</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file1</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)){</span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>    st_read</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">file1$datapath</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\">    <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># this reactive output contains the summary of the dataset and display the summary in table format</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  output$filedf </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderPlot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#008\">if</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#008\">is</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#008\">null</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())){</span><span style=\"color:#008\">return</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">()}</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    plot</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  output$map </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderLeaflet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    leaflet</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">())</span><span style=\"color:#000\">  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> addTiles</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">%&gt;%</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> <br>      addPolygons</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># the following renderUI is used to dynamically generate the tabsets when the file is loaded. Until the file is loaded, app will not show the tabset.</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  output$tb </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> renderUI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">({</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      tabsetPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">tabPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;About file&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> plotOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;filedf&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>                  tabPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Map&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> leafletOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;map&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">})</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>ui.R</div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px;word-wrap:break-word\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">shiny</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>shinyUI</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fluidPage</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  titlePanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;File Input&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>  sidebarLayout</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    sidebarPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      fileInput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;file&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Upload the file&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> multiple</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#800\"># fileinput() function is used to get the file upload contorl option</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      helpText</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;Default max. file size is 5MB&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      tags$hr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">()</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    mainPanel</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>      uiOutput</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&quot;tb&quot;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>    <br>  </span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;Shiny - Web Framework for R&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">shiny-discus...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br>\r\nTo view this discussion on the web visit <a href=\"https://groups.google.com/d/msgid/shiny-discuss/4cbd35f9-4770-49